  "id": "COMPOUND:43509 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Akuammigine is implicated in the biological activity of SCCH-26 through a multi-step pathway involving the MIP (methyl-4-phenyl-1,3-benzodiazepine) and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Akuammigine directly targets MIP, which in turn is a target of both Sophoradiol and Propenyl propyl disulfide. These compounds are all linked to SCCH-26, indicating a potential mechanism by which Akuammigine influences the cell line. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway suggests a complex interaction, possibly involving the activation of downstream signaling pathways that ultimately affect SCCH-26. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of MIP as a central mediator in the relationship between Akuammigine and SCCH-26, with the exact mechanism of action remaining to be fully elucidated.",
